{"name":"Espalier","hex":"#2f5f3a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"espalier","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A latticework used to shape or train the branches of a tree or shrub into a two-dimensional ornamental or useful design, as along a wall or fence.","A plant that has been shaped in this manner."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To train a plant in this manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/espalier"}],"entries":[{"title":"Espalier","blocks":[{"text":"Espalier is the horticultural and ancient agricultural practice of controlling woody plant growth for the production of fruit, by pruning and tying branches to a frame. Plants are frequently shaped in formal patterns, flat against a structure such as a wall, fence, or trellis. The term is also used to refer to plants which have been shaped in this way."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Horizontal_espalier.JPG/330px-Horizontal_espalier.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Espalier","wikidata":"Q1754876"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Espalier_fruit_tree_at_Standen%2C_West_Sussex%2C_England_May_2006.JPG/500px-Espalier_fruit_tree_at_Standen%2C_West_Sussex%2C_England_May_2006.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Espalier_fruit_tree_at_Standen%2C_West_Sussex%2C_England_May_2006.JPG/1280px-Espalier_fruit_tree_at_Standen%2C_West_Sussex%2C_England_May_2006.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Espalier_fruit_tree_at_Standen%2C_West_Sussex%2C_England_May_2006.JPG/500px-Espalier_fruit_tree_at_Standen%2C_West_Sussex%2C_England_May_2006.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt